WEBVTT

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.930
I can't accept this.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.840
Then what about Ibuki?

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.310
Yagami, you go home
with your father.

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:43.420
Why won't you
take it, Mr. Godai?

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.870
The truth is, I want this
letter of introduction

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.540
more than anything.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.170
But I can't accept it.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.170
I'm afraid this may take me
somewhere I don't want to be.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:58.360
I want to choose my
own path to my future.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.920
It's my life, after all

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:02.900
Mr. Godai?

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.380
All right kids!
I'll take you ALL on!

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.630
C'mon!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.520
I'm gonna get you!

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:35.660
Godai!

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:39.860
Ouch!

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.170
Godai! I got it!
I got a job!

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.610
I got a job with
Mirage Industries!

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.480
Director Yagami's letter
of introduction worked!

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:53.420
He actually gave you
that letter?

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.220
That's great, Sakamoto!

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.320
Thanks.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:19.670
Isn't it nice to
have Ibuki home again?

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.850
It was a long month.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:32.290
I wonder why Godai
refused your letter?

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.890
Who cares about him. He brought me
nothing but grief.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.730
You know that.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.440
W-Well, but still

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.980
I don't even want
to hear his name!

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.330
I wonder what he meant

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.380
when he said he wanted
to choose his own path?

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:53.850
I don't know.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.110
Maybe I've become
a pain in his butt.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.980
Maybe Mr. Godai got tired.
You're pretty persistent, Yagami.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.690
Why don't you go talk to him?

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.320
He might be regretting
what he said.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.500
You should! You even
left home to try to help.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.670
You should talk to him.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.230
Cheers!

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.000
Great!

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.210
Beer hasn't tasted this good
since I got into college!

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:34.740
I can't believe you
actually wrangled that letter

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.420
out of Director Yagami.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.690
I was desperate.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.530
I knew if I missed that chance..

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.980
You're not regretting
what you did..?

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:51.130
You better not
hate me later.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.170
You better not
come crying to me

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.710
when your company goes under.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:58.670
Mirage Industries sounds like
a company that would just disappear.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.980
S-Sakamoto, I'm Just kidding!

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.160
You heard what
Yagami's dad said.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.310
He said he selected
that company

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.480
and that he'd guarantee
that it won't go bankrupt.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.360
Gotcha!

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.910
Let's drink and party tonight!
It's on me!

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.690
We'd like five
or six more beers,

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.500
and keep 'em flowing!

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.020
I also want shochu and tonic
with lemon and oolong tea.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.850
Strawberries, tomatoes,
melons, green apples,

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.790
plums, oranges, cucumbers,
avocados, whatever.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.030
And reserve me a bottle
to keep here!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.970
One more beer!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.300
C'mon, Godai. Hurry up.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.810
I'll be right there!

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.480
So that's it.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.650
Godai--?

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.250
What?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:22.550
He said Sakamoto got a job.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:26.770
So he might stay out with him
all night, drinking?

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:27.770
Yes.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.770
He's so happy-go-lucky.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.470
Thank you! Please come again!

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:43.040
Godai, let's go
somewhere else.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.520
Somewhere else?

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:48.940
A cabaret!

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:51.310
I know someone
who works at one.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.860
He can introduce us
to some nice girls.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:56.860
You sure love
introductions, don't you?

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:58.530
Got a problem with that?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:10.430
So let's toast to
your new job, Mr. Student!

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:12.500
Thank you!

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:14.940
Four more beers here, please!

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.420
And some smoked cuttlefish
hors d'oeuvres!

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.310
Your generosity will surely
get you far in life.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:23.280
That's right.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.680
This guy has the most
incredible connection.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.810
I don't know what
Godai is thinking.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:49.720
He never came home
last night, did he?

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:53.660
He was celebrating
Sakamoto's employment

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.690
I know, but does he
really have the time

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.680
to be celebrating
for other people?

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.940
He's too happy-go-lucky.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.970
His future wife
will have a hard life.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:07.840
I don't know about that, but work is
something he'll have to do for life.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.560
He should take the time
to find one that suits him.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:12.500
But it's already October.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.560
He really should have taken
that letter of introduction.

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.860
If only he had that,

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:20.470
even good-for-nothing
Godai could have.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:25.520
Please! Godai is doing the very best
he can in his own way.

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.720
I think.

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:43.730
Sakamoto!

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:46.700
Hey! Sakamoto!

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.730
It's open.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.110
It reeks in here.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.950
I knew you were sleeping.
GET UP!

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:04.750
What is it?

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:09.620
Don't "what is it?" me!
Get up already.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.250
M-Mr. Ioka?

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:15.730
C'mon! Get up and
get ready to work.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:17.120
Get ready?

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:19.760
Don't play dumb.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.360
You promised last night

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.630
that you'd work to
pay off what you owe.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:27.220
I-I don't remember that. You?

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:29.500
Give up the charade. C'mon!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.350
Just come as you are.
Don't be late.

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:36.360
Late?! Oh no!

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:39.090
Where do you think
you're going?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:42.280
Where else?!
To the preschool!

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.150
Idiot! Don't talk nonsense!

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:45.100
No.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:59.210
Yagami? How did it go?

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.550
They told me
he's not here.

00:10:01.610 --> 00:10:03.710
He's not? And we came
all the way here.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:06.610
I wonder if he's
job-hunting?

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:10.250
I don't know. They said
he never called in.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.560
Sick, maybe?

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:14.060
Car accident?

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:15.360
Kidnapped?

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:17.560
N-No way.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:33.810
Until you pay back what you owe,
I'm going to work you hard.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:34.850
You better be prepared.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.080
Yes, sir.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.580
I can't hear you!

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:40.630
YES, SIR!

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:45.650
All right. To draw in customers,
we must smile and articulate.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:46.600
Say it

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:51.020
Yes! To draw in customers,
we must smile and articulate!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.610
Good. Remember
what you Just said.

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.260
That's our company motto.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:57.840
Huh?

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.090
Smile!

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:03.970
Now we will begin
your practical training.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.180
Practical...

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:08.110
...training?

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:10.870
Sir! You there, sir!

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.270
Sir, please take advantage of
our special offer and experience paradise!

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:15.140
N-No.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.090
Please! Just give us a try.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.990
You're here to have
a good time, aren't you?

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:20.220
W-Well

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:23.100
Please show these
two gentlemen in!

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:29.800
Now you try.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:30.730
Uh.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.360
C'mon, wake up!

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:34.610
Do it. Jeez.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.310
W-What'll we do?

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.820
We gotta do it, I guess.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.820
C'mon ! Talk to 'em!

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:45.840
Um..

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.150
That cabaret over there.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:50.780
we have a special
offer now, and um..

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:51.750
What did you say?

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.060
We have a special offer
over at that cabaret.

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:59.730
Idiot! Don't talk to couples!

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:02.700
And what's with
your dismal attitude? Huh?!

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.130
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:07.630
Look at Sakamoto.
He's doing all right.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:10.810
How about it, sir?!
We've got some great girls!

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.220
Don't be shy.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:14.870
Never mind me..

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:19.560
No, Sakamoto!
He's our regular customer.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:21.520
How nice to see you,

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.380
Mr. Executive from
Mirage Industries!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.990
Please come in, sir.
Lisa is waiting for you.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.390
Hey.. Isn't Mirage Industries
the place that hired you?

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:36.830
This isn't good.
He's a regular here?

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:44.580
What's up?

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.500
I'm sorry! I'll leave
Godai here with you.

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:49.740
Please!

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.690
What?!

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:54.050
H-Hey!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.860
Hold it! What's the idea?

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.610
You're going
to run, too? Huh?!

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:03.970
No way...!

00:13:27.420 --> 00:13:28.470
Godai?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.060
Good morning.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:33.090
How's your job search going?

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:37.380
I'm on my way to see
my career counselor again.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.430
I see. You're trying so hard.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:44.120
You look a little
run down. Are you okay?

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:49.100
M-Me? S-Sure.
I'm fine. I'm off!

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:03.610
I didn't have to lie to her.
What am I doing?

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.300
Y-Yagami?

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:30.260
I'm so glad you weren't sick.

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:32.440
What do you mean?

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.450
I dropped by the preschool yesterday,

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.510
and they told me
you took a day off.

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:41.980
Oh. But as you
can see, I'm fine.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.460
How's your job hunt going?

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.380
Okay.

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:50.800
Um..

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:57.470
I'm sorry, but there's
somewhere I need to go.

00:14:58.550 --> 00:14:59.340
Sorry about that.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.070
Then see you next time.

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:03.910
Sure.

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.680
I'm really sorry.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.640
I-It's okay.

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:09.880
See you.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:11.240
Yes.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:20.620
Maybe he does think
I'm a pain in the butt.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:33.710
To draw in customers,
we must smile and articulate.

00:15:34.340 --> 00:15:35.360
One more time!

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:39.840
Yes! To draw in customers,
we must smile and articulate.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.880
Good! Let's see that
enthusiasm again today!

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:43.600
Yes!

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:47.110
Please check us out!
We have special pricing!

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:48.350
Come in! Come in!

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:52.660
Right now, come in and have
all you can eat and drink

00:15:52.730 --> 00:15:55.330
for a special price!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.010
Sir!

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:59.040
You're not bad when you
put your mind to it.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.540
You think so? I have
to work hard enough

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.620
to cover for
Sakamoto, after all

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:06.300
You've got the right attitude!

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:11.000
Right attitude. Sure.

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.340
I'm just desperate!

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:16.740
Come on in!
We've got young girls!

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:19.320
It's all-you-can-eat and drink
for an unbelievably low price!

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:21.960
Sir! You, sir!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.140
Yes?

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:29.220
What in the world
are you up to?

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:30.590
W-Well

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.290
Hey!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.700
Don't walk away from him!
Show him in!

00:16:41.740 --> 00:16:45.000
Please show me in.

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:49.600
You're Godai's next-door neighbor?

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:51.590
- We'll have to take care of you!
- Go ahead and order!

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:56.380
Whatever you want.
It's all on Godai!

00:16:57.260 --> 00:16:59.960
When did I ever
say it's on me?

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:02.060
Manager!

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.760
W-What are you talking about?

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.930
You want me to tell her

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.410
that you're working
at a cabaret

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:11.990
instead of looking
for a real job?

00:17:13.310 --> 00:17:16.070
Bring five or six
bottles here, won't you?!

00:17:16.150 --> 00:17:19.470
I'm going to drink
til closing tonight!

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:36.780
Yotsuya, remember your promise.
Not a word to the manager.

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:41.970
Get off my case.
Can't you trust me?

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:58.950
Open quietly.

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:06.580
Why are you acting
so nervous, Godai?

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.930
Remember, not a word.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:10.050
Welcome home.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.550
You two were out together?
How unusual.

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:16.200
As a matter of fact,
we were at a ca-

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:16.970
Yotsuya!

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:19.060
Caviar is delicious.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.380
Are you drunk?

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:24.730
H-He's so drunk.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:27.000
Let's go upstairs.

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:29.350
-- Um...
-- Yes?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:32.510
How did your meeting with
your career counselor go?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.150
Oh, yes.

00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:38.620
Don't worry.
He's pretty much set

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:42.200
A service-oriented
line of work, was it, Godai?

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:48.030
You're making no sense.
Let's go to sleep.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.360
Are we sleeping together?

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.270
Of course not

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:52.960
I can't tonight

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:05.080
If his job search
isn't going well,

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.810
he might be
embarrassed to see you.

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:09.630
I wonder. Seems like he's
avoiding you every time.

00:19:09.700 --> 00:19:10.960
Maybe it's time
to call it quits.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.220
It doesn't matter
what you all say.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:14.850
Yagami's going to
see this through

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:18.490
until Mr. Godai gets
a job. Right?

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:20.940
How sweet.

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:28.680
Come in! We have special
pricing for tonight only!

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:32.180
Sir! Experience paradise
for a special price!

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:35.010
Is it true that
we can drink for free?

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:38.010
Sure. I have a friend
who works here.

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.740
Hey! It's Godai!

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.050
What're you doing here?

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:49.820
Yotsuya! You promised!

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:53.910
Don't worry. I didn't say
a word to the manager.

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:08.110
Hey. You're sure I can deduct
their bill off your pay?

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:11.650
Godai, why don't you
drink, too?

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:14.390
Whose money do you think
you're using?! Whose?!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:18.780
Akemi, you're wanted
at table six.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.320
Yes!

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:25.220
How old are you, Akemi?

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:26.260
Seventeen.

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.100
Really?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.100
Hello there. I'm Akemi.

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:35.740
Your outfit's so cute!
I'd love to wear that, too!

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:37.800
I bet you'd look
great in this.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.530
Thank you!

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.510
Godai, maybe I'll
work here, too!

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:44.580
Do whatever you want!

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:53.100
Damn them freeloaders!

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:57.360
Maybe I should just
tell Manager about this.

00:20:57.830 --> 00:20:59.170
No, I can't!

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:03.830
She thinks I've been busy
tying to get a real job.

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:07.210
Godai, thanks!

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.970
You better come home soon.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:14.730
Wait! This is a secret you
have to keep from the manager.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:15.470
Is that clear?

00:21:15.550 --> 00:21:18.040
It's okay with us.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.240
Do you want us to tell her
in a subtle way?

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:23.120
I'm not good at subtlety.

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:24.420
Neither am I

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.220
Neither am I

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:30.200
No thank you. I'll tell her
myself when the time comes.

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:32.290
Please do, or
we'd feel awkward.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:36.430
Yeah. We can't keep
imposing on you every night

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.570
You're going to swindle me
every night?

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.230
You're making us sound bad!

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:46.000
What a delicious secret, Godai.

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:49.600
We're back!

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:53.310
Good evening.

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:58.980
You weren't with
Godai tonight?

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:03.050
He must be running around,
job hunting.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.160
With a yellow sash
around his head, perhaps.

00:22:07.710 --> 00:22:09.370
Am I missing something?

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:12.210
Why don't we have
a drink, Manager?

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:14.880
Sit down.

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:16.400
Here?

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:21.500
C'mon ! Here's to Godai's
future employment! Cheers!

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:22.470
Cheers!

00:22:22.550 --> 00:22:23.980
Cheers.

00:22:24.050 --> 00:22:25.810
Come in! Eat and
drink all you want!

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:28.660
Akemi, you're wanted
at Table Six!

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:30.470
Yes!

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:45.440
Damn! I always
work diligently.

00:22:45.500 --> 00:22:46.670
I know. I know.

00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:48.330
No, you don't!

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:53.450
Why does this always
happen to me?

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:55.210
Yeah. Yeah.

00:22:55.280 --> 00:22:56.540
Don't you agree?

00:22:56.780 --> 00:22:58.540
I do. I do.

00:23:07.330 --> 00:23:07.980
I'm leaving.

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:11.250
Thanks. That'll
be 2,800 yen.

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:16.370
I don't have enough.

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:23.900
Come in! It's delicious,
but cheap!

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:27.410
Sir! Come on in!
Delicious oden!

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:31.350
You're good at this. I need
you to make 500 more yen.

00:23:31.820 --> 00:23:34.350
I'm a professional, you know.

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:38.580
Sir! You there, sir!
How about some great oden?!

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:43.930
Come in! Come in and have
some delicious oden!

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.130
Sir! Sir!

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:51.330
Fired from preschool?!

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:54.010
Then where has he been eating.

00:23:54.080 --> 00:23:56.750
those homemade lunches?

00:23:56.810 --> 00:23:59.300
Godai, you better
fess up like a man!

00:23:59.380 --> 00:24:03.810
Next: "I'm So Sorry, Kyoko.
I Don't Deserve to Eat Your Lunch"

00:24:03.990 --> 00:24:06.650
But don't you quit
that cabaret, okay?
